# CMS and public content

## Collections (src/payload.config.ts)
- `pages` — home (`pageKind: home` → `/`), legal (`pageKind: legal` → `/{slug}`), default landing blocks
- `services` — public URLs `/{slug}` (air-duct-cleaning, dryer-vent-cleaning, combo)
- `locations` — `/locations/{slug}`
- `posts` — blog; rewrite `/blog` → `/posts`
- `leads` — contact form submissions (`POST /api/contact`); public create, admin read
- `media`, `categories`, `users`
## Globals: `header`, `footer`, `site-settings`
- Header/Footer = portable chrome (brand mark text|logo|both, nav/columns). No `showOffices`-style fields.
- Project-specific links (offices, cities) are seeded as normal column/nav links.

## Where copy lives
- Live CMS is source of truth after seed.
- Defaults/seed: `src/content/*`, `src/seed/amazonadc.ts`, `src/seed/blog-and-legal.ts`.
- Frontend mappers: `src/utilities/{home,services,locations,legal,blog}.ts`.
- Header/Footer are **portable chrome** (brand + nav/columns). Project-specific links live in seed, not field names. See `.cursor/rules/reusable-cms-chrome.mdc`.
- After field changes: `npm run generate:types` (writes `src/payload-types.ts`).

## Contact / spam
Honeypot field `website`, in-memory rate limit, optional Cloudflare Turnstile. Leads status: `new | contacted | closed | spam`.

## Routing
`src/app/(frontend)/[slug]/page.tsx` resolves service, legal page, or CMS page. Keep redirects in `redirects.ts` plus Payload redirects plugin. Rebuild after changing plugin `from` URLs.
